/* Descriptors for a whole set-aside list, disambiguated.
   Date and time to the minute is enough for almost every pair of copies, but
   two set-asides made within the same minute produce identical labels AND
   identical accessible names — leaving the athlete unable to tell which copy
   they are about to delete. The internal stamp differs, and must stay internal.

   So a "Copy N" suffix is added ONLY to rows whose formatted label collides,
   numbered oldest-first within that group. Not seconds: two operations can
   share a second too, and seconds are noise on every ordinary row.

   Returns one descriptor per input record, in the caller's order, so numbering
   recomputes naturally on rerender after a deletion. */
